---
id: crispy-garlic-soy-glazed-tofu
title: Crispy Garlic-Soy Glazed Tofu
category: modular_protein

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 320

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: false

---

Press: drain @extra-firm-tofu{1%package} and wrap it in a clean kitchen towel or 3 layers of paper towel. Set a plate on top and weigh it down with a heavy skillet or a large can. Press for ~press-time{15%min} (15 to 20 minutes), then cut the block into 2 cm cubes.

Season and starch: preheat the convection #oven to 205°C (400°F). In a mixing bowl, toss the cubes gently with @soy-sauce-less-sodium{1%tbsp} and 1 tsp of @avocado-oil{1%tsp} until the liquid is absorbed. Dust with @cornstarch{1.5%tbsp}, @garlic-powder{1/4%tsp}, and @black-pepper{1/4%tsp}, and toss until every cube has a matte, powdery coat with no dry starch left in the bowl.

Bake: spread the cubes in a single layer on a parchment-lined #sheet-pan with space between them so they roast rather than steam. Bake for ~bake-time{25%min}, flipping at 15 minutes, until deeply golden and crisp; check the last few minutes so the edges don't burn.

Glaze: while the tofu bakes, stir @cornstarch{1/2%tsp} into 1 tbsp of cold water. In a small #saucepan over medium heat, combine @soy-sauce-less-sodium{2%tbsp}, 1 tsp of @sesame-oil{1%tsp}, 1 tbsp of @rice-vinegar{1%tbsp}, 1 tbsp of @maple-syrup{1%tbsp}, @fresh-garlic{2%clove} finely minced, @ground-ginger{1/4%tsp}, and the slurry. Simmer for ~glaze-time{90%sec} (60 to 90 seconds) until glossy and thick like syrup.

Toss: take the pan off the heat, add the hot tofu, and toss for 10 seconds to coat evenly. Sprinkle with @green-onions{1/4%bunch}, thinly sliced. Divide equally into 2 meal prep containers (about 160 g per portion).
